  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Somatrogon is a long-acting growth hormone analogue used to treat growth disorders in children. It is authorised in the European Union as a newer medicine, and is also still under investigation for further uses.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q110220159\">Wikidata Q110220159</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>somatrogon</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>H01AC08</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB14960\">DB14960</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q110220159\">Q110220159</a></td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>30465.1 g/mol (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
end Somatrogon;
